    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "annot-005",
      "table_id": "table-003",
      "annotation_marker": "5",
      "annotation_type": "footnote",
      "annotation_text": "Footnote not printed in the source (Table 9 prints only footnotes 1-3). Table 9 is the Extended-Visit-Cycle variant of the Main Study, this corresponds to Table 7 (Main Study) footnote 10: \"SAEs recorded up to 30 days after study treatment discontinuation.\" Mapping confirmed by clinical review (2026-08-15): §7.4.3 lists \"AEs (SAEs recorded 30 days post study treatment discontinuation)\".",
      "annotation_scope": "cell",
      "referenced_elements": {
        "property_ids": [],
        "column_ids": [],
        "activity_ids": [],
        "cell_references": [
          {
            "activity_id": "act-004",
            "column_id": "col-005"
          }
        ]
      },
      "marker_locations": [
        {
          "table_number": 3,
          "location_type": "schedule_cell",
          "row_position": 7,
          "column_position": 5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "annot-006",
      "table_id": "table-003",
      "annotation_marker": "6",
      "annotation_type": "footnote",
      "annotation_text": "Footnote not printed in the source (Table 9 prints only footnotes 1-3). Table 9 is the Extended-Visit-Cycle variant of the Main Study, so this most likely corresponds to Table 7 (Main Study) footnote 12: \"If dose interruption or modification is required at any point on study because of hematologic toxicity, weekly blood draws for CBC will be monitored until the adverse event resolves, and to ensure safety of the new dose, weekly blood draws for CBC will be also be required for an additional 4 weeks after the adverse event has been resolved to the specified levels, after which monitoring every 4 weeks may resume.\" Clinical review 2026-08-15: hypothesis retained; §7.4 does not restate this rule.",
      "annotation_scope": "activity",
      "referenced_elements": {
        "property_ids": [],
        "column_ids": [],
        "activity_ids": [
          "act-007"
        ],
        "cell_references": []
      },
      "marker_locations": [
        {
          "table_number": 3,
          "location_type": "activity_name",
          "row_position": 10
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "annot-007",
      "table_id": "table-003",
      "annotation_marker": "7",
      "annotation_type": "footnote",
      "annotation_text": "Footnote not printed in the source (Table 9 prints only footnotes 1-3). Table 9 is the Extended-Visit-Cycle variant of the Main Study, so this most likely corresponds to Table 7 (Main Study) footnote 13: \"CA-125 levels must be normal at screening or > 90% decrease as compared with baseline prior to last platinum-based chemotherapy course. Abnormal CA-125 levels during study do not represent disease progression; however, they may prompt imaging if clinically indicated. CA-125 sample within 72 hours of dose on Cycle 1/Day 1.\" Clinical review 2026-08-15: hypothesis retained; note the screening and Cycle 1/Day 1 clauses of footnote 13 are phase-specific and may not apply in extended cycles; §7.4 is silent on CA-125 rules.",
      "annotation_scope": "activity",
      "referenced_elements": {
        "property_ids": [],
        "column_ids": [],
        "activity_ids": [
          "act-008"
        ],
        "cell_references": []
      },
      "marker_locations": [
        {
          "table_number": 3,
          "location_type": "activity_name",
          "row_position": 11
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "annot-008",
      "table_id": "table-003",
      "annotation_marker": "8",
      "annotation_type": "footnote",
      "annotation_text": "Footnote not printed in the source (Table 9 prints only footnotes 1-3). Table 9 is the Extended-Visit-Cycle variant of the Main Study, so this most likely corresponds to Table 7 (Main Study) footnote 14: \"For determination of CA-125 progression, at least 2 CA-125 values at least 1 week apart are required for confirmation (Section 6.1).\" Clinical review 2026-08-15: hypothesis retained; content is phase-independent; §7.4 does not restate it.",
      "annotation_scope": "activity",
      "referenced_elements": {
        "property_ids": [],
        "column_ids": [],
        "activity_ids": [
          "act-008"
        ],
        "cell_references": []
      },
      "marker_locations": [
        {
          "table_number": 3,
          "location_type": "activity_name",
          "row_position": 11
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "annot-009",
      "table_id": "table-003",
      "annotation_marker": "9",
      "annotation_type": "footnote",
      "annotation_text": "Footnote not printed in the source (Table 9 prints only footnotes 1-3). Table 9 is the Extended-Visit-Cycle variant of the Main Study, this corresponds to Table 7 (Main Study) footnote 16: \"Patients will have a 12-lead ECG at Screening, Baseline (predose, within 30 minutes), 2 hours postdose on Day 1(within 30 minutes), Cycle 2/Day 1, (predose, 2 hours postdose, within 30 minutes) and upon study treatment discontinuation. Note that the ECG is to be completed prior to the PK blood draw.\" Mapping confirmed by clinical review (2026-08-15): §7.4.3 lists 12-lead ECG at study treatment discontinuation — the only ECG mark in this table; the screening/PK clauses of footnote 16 do not apply in extended cycles.",
      "annotation_scope": "activity",
      "referenced_elements": {
        "property_ids": [],
        "column_ids": [],
        "activity_ids": [
          "act-009"
        ],
        "cell_references": []
      },
      "marker_locations": [
        {
          "table_number": 3,
          "location_type": "activity_name",
          "row_position": 12
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "annot-010",
      "table_id": "table-003",
      "annotation_marker": "10",
      "annotation_type": "footnote",
      "annotation_text": "Footnote not printed in the source (Table 9 prints only footnotes 1-3). Table 9 is the Extended-Visit-Cycle variant of the Main Study, so this most likely corresponds to Table 7 (Main Study) footnote 22: \"RECIST tumor assessment via CT or MRI scan of abdomen/pelvis and clinically indicated areas required at baseline, then after every 2 cycles (ie, 8 weeks with a window of ± 7 days from date of visit) through Cycle 14 (56 weeks), then after every 6 cycles (24 weeks with a window of ± 7 days) until study treatment discontinuation; at this point, a final follow-up set of imaging is required. PET/CT may be used according to RECIST guidelines. Cycle timing will not be delayed for treatment interruptions, and tumor assessment should occur according to this schedule regardless of whether study treatment is interrupted. If a patient discontinues treatment for clinical progression and does not meet the criteria specified in the protocol, scans and CA-125 testing should continue at the specified intervals until progression is confirmed or until the start of subsequent anticancer treatment.\" NOTE (clinical review 2026-08-15): §7.4.2 states RECIST \"after every 2 cycles through Cycle 14 and then after every 3 cycles\", which conflicts with footnote 22's post-Cycle-14 cadence of every 6 cycles (24 weeks) — a source-internal contradiction, left unresolved; hypothesis retained.",
      "annotation_scope": "activity",
      "referenced_elements": {
        "property_ids": [],
        "column_ids": [],
        "activity_ids": [
          "act-010"
        ],
        "cell_references": []
      },
      "marker_locations": [
        {
          "table_number": 3,
          "location_type": "activity_name",
          "row_position": 13
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "annot-011",
      "table_id": "table-003",
      "annotation_marker": "11",
      "annotation_type": "footnote",
      "annotation_text": "Footnote not printed in the source (Table 9 prints only footnotes 1-3). Table 9 is the Extended-Visit-Cycle variant of the Main Study, this corresponds to Table 7 (Main Study) footnote 24: \"PROs (FOSI, EQ-5D-5L, neuropathy questionnaire) will be collected while on study treatment every 8 weeks through the first year, then every 12 weeks thereafter. If the patient discontinues study treatment, assessment will occur at that time and then 8 weeks (± 2 weeks) later, regardless of status of subsequent treatment. PROs should be administered before conducting any other procedures.\" Mapping confirmed by clinical review (2026-08-15): §7.4.2 states PROs every 3 cycles (= every 12 weeks, matching footnote 24) and repeats \"PROs should be administered before conducting any other procedures\" verbatim; §7.4.4 matches the 8 (± 2) weeks post-discontinuation assessment.",
      "annotation_scope": "activity",
      "referenced_elements": {
        "property_ids": [],
